### Digital Wallet & Flash-Sale Engine — API Collection (VS Code "REST Client" format)
### Usage: install the "REST Client" VS Code extension, open this file, click "Send Request"
### above each block. Variables below are shared across all requests in this file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@customerEmail = customer1@example.com
@customerPassword = StrongP@ssw0rd
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@adminPassword = StrongP@ssw0rd

### After running "Login (customer)" / "Login (admin)" below, copy the tokens from the
### response into these two lines (REST Client also lets you chain requests with
### {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.accessToken}} if you prefer — kept explicit here
### for portability with Postman/Bruno imports).
@customerAccessToken = PASTE_CUSTOMER_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@customerRefreshToken = PASTE_CUSTOMER_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE
@adminAccessToken = PASTE_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

@productId = PASTE_PRODUCT_ID_HERE
@flashSaleEventId = PASTE_FLASH_SALE_EVENT_ID_HERE
@otherUserId = PASTE_RECIPIENT_USER_ID_HERE


########################################
# HEALTH
########################################

### Health check (db + redis + queue)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


########################################
# AUTH
########################################

### Register a new CUSTOMER account
# @name registerCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### Register a second account (to use as a transfer recipient / to promote to ADMIN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### Login (customer)
# @name loginCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### Login (admin) — the account must already have role=ADMIN in the DB
# (see README "Creating the first admin user")
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### Refresh access/refresh token pair
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{customerRefreshToken}}"
}

### Logout (revoke a refresh token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{customerRefreshToken}}"
}

### Get current authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAccessToken}}

### [RBAC demo] ADMIN-only endpoint — 200 for an admin token, 403 for a customer token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/admin-check
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}


########################################
# WALLET
########################################

### Deposit funds into the current user's wallet
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 100.50
}

### Get current user's wallet balance + recent ledger entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/me?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAccessToken}}

### Transfer funds to another user (idempotent — resending the same idempotencyKey
### returns the original result instead of transferring again)
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toUserId": "{{otherUserId}}",
  "amount": 25.00,
  "idempotencyKey": "transfer-demo-0001"
}


########################################
# FLASH SALE
########################################

### [ADMIN] Create a flash-sale event for a seeded product
### (run `npm run seed` first to get a productId — see README)
POST {{baseUrl}}/flash-sale/events
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "totalStock": 10,
  "startsAt": "2026-09-03T00:00:00.000Z",
  "endsAt": "2026-12-31T23:59:59.000Z"
}

### [ADMIN] Get a flash-sale event's status and remaining stock
GET {{baseUrl}}/flash-sale/events/{{flashSaleEventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

### Purchase one unit from a flash-sale event (idempotent via idempotencyKey)
POST {{baseUrl}}/flash-sale/purchase
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{flashSaleEventId}}",
  "idempotencyKey": "purchase-demo-0001"
}
